Error: SHELLCHECK_WARNING (CWE-563):
/usr/bin/antlr-config:6:1: warning[SC2034]: datadir appears unused. Verify use (or export if used externally).
#    4|   prefix=/usr
#    5|   exec_prefix=/usr
#    6|-> datadir=/usr/share
#    7|   libdir=/usr/lib64
#    8|   includedir=/usr/include
Only libdir and includedir are used later in the script.  datadir is a leftover of the configure-generated prefix block, so this is a harmless dead assignment.

Error: SHELLCHECK_WARNING (CWE-563):
/usr/bin/antlr-config:37:6: warning[SC2034]: optarg appears unused. Verify use (or export if used externally).
#   35|   	case "$1" in
#   36|   		-*=*) optarg=`echo "$1" | sed 's/[-_a-zA-Z0-9]*=//'` ;;
#   37|-> 		*) optarg= ;;
#   38|   	esac
#   39|   
The script only tests which option was given and never works with its value, so optarg is assigned but never read.  This is a harmless dead assignment.

Error: SHELLCHECK_WARNING:
/usr/bin/antlr-config:56:12: warning[SC2194]: This word is constant. Did you forget the $ on a variable?
#   54|         ;;
#   55|   	--libs)
#   56|->       case gcc in
#   57|           cl|bcc32)
#   58|             libs="${libdir}/antlr.lib"
The word is a literal compiler name that is tested on purpose, not a variable reference, so no '$' is missing here.
